findings.body:
The PR changes the message in `WryWebviewDispatcher::delete_cookie` from `DeleteCookie` to `SetCookie`. `Webview::delete_cookie` and `WebviewWindow::delete_cookie` now set the cookie rather than removing it. The event loop handler still has a separate `DeleteCookie` arm, but nothing constructs that variant now.

::diff{file="crates/tauri-runtime-wry/src/lib.rs" lines="1712-1720"}

::callout{type="warning"}
The diff hunk only shows the `set_cookie` side, so this is the wrong direction. Compare with `set_cookie` on lines 1700-1710, which correctly sends `SetCookie`. The `delete_cookie` function should send `DeleteCookie`.

Because `WebviewMessage::DeleteCookie` now has no constructor, rustc's `dead_code` lint will likely warn about it. That is a problem for CI builds that deny warnings.

The mock runtime (`crates/tauri/src/test/mock_runtime.rs:649`) doesn't cover this path, so nothing in the test suite catches it.

The body of `window_features` has extra spacing in `inner_size(size.width,    size.height)` and no space after the comma in `position(position.x,position.y)`. That fails `cargo fmt --check`, which Tauri's CI runs. The size and position calls were also swapped compared with the old `with_window_features`. Both calls only set builder fields, so the swap is probably harmless, but it isn't explained.

